From a28a787730c3d7fcf2ad6e11f1886d537dab9075 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Akhilesh Samineni <akhilesh.samineni@broadcom.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Apr 2021 13:21:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] bgpd: set scope for IPv6 link-local update-source

Set sin6_scope_id from the selected interface before binding a BGP
socket to an IPv6 link-local source address. This preserves the
SONiC-carried behavior on FRR 10.7.1 and avoids ambiguous link-local
binds.

Original SONiC patch commit: 92ab2d74fca06f86c00d886ac249f7f2d89e93fe

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Signed-off-by: Deepak Singhal <deepsinghal@microsoft.com>
---
 bgpd/bgp_network.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/bgpd/bgp_network.c b/bgpd/bgp_network.c
index 6178213d7e..ef2675dc20 100644
--- a/bgpd/bgp_network.c
+++ b/bgpd/bgp_network.c
@@ -802,6 +802,11 @@ int bgp_update_address(struct interface *ifp, const union sockunion *dst,
 		return 1;
 
 	prefix2sockunion(sel, addr);
+
+	if (IN6_IS_ADDR_LINKLOCAL(&addr->sin6.sin6_addr)) {
+		addr->sin6.sin6_scope_id = ifp->ifindex;
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
